From e2a37475676cacba89859680e6151258ec04720b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:33:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Subsonic/OpenSubsonic (Navidrome) music source

Imports the songs of a Subsonic compatible server into the collection so
they show up in the Albums, Artists and Tracks views and can be played
and queued like local files.

- SubsonicListener lists the server (search3 with an empty query on
  OpenSubsonic servers, getAlbumList2 + getAlbum otherwise) and feeds
  DatabaseInterface::insertTracksList/removeTracksList like the file
  indexer. Tracks are only removed after a complete listing, so an
  offline server keeps its tracks.
- Tracks are stored with a credential free stream URL
  (rest/stream.view?id=..&format=raw, never transcoded); token
  authentication (md5(password + salt), API 1.13.0+) is added with a
  fresh salt when the URL is played.
- Cover art is served by an image://subsonic/ provider (getCoverArt,
  cached on disk) and exported to MPRIS as an authenticated URL. A
  runnable on the provider's pool fetches the cover and hands it to the
  response through a queued connection, so the response emits finished()
  on the pixmap reader thread that owns and deletes it; responses whose
  delegate scrolled away skip the download.
- Plays are scrobbled (now playing on start, submission on finish).
- Playback errors of remote tracks no longer remove them from the
  database, and the local file indexer leaves non local URLs alone.
- Settings: server URL, user name and password.
